cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Multimodal Benchmark of Classical, Machine Learning, and Foundation
  Models for ERCOT Electricity Price Forecasting
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rohan
    family-names: Fozdar
    affiliation: Knox College
abstract: >-
  A multimodal benchmark of classical, machine-learning, deep-learning,
  foundation, and hybrid models for retrospective hourly ERCOT
  electricity-price estimation and spike detection. The engineered matrix
  has 77,956 hourly observations and 87 model features covering 2016 to
  2024. Twelve configurations are compared. The consolidated project
  benchmark reports a Chronos--XGBoost hybrid as the lowest-error
  configuration. Manuscript in preparation.
keywords:
  - electricity price forecasting
  - ERCOT
  - price spikes
  - time series foundation models
  - news sentiment
  - gradient boosting
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/rohanfozdar/Electricity-Price-Forecaster
year: 2026
